text , comment nodes, and processing instruction nodes must be ignored when establishing whether an element's contents match the element's content model or not, and must be ignored when following algorithms that define document and element semantics.
link "Inter-element whitespace" #inter-element-whitespace
text Thus, an element  is said to be  by a second element  if  and  have the same parent node and there are no other element nodes or  nodes (other than ) between them. Similarly, a node is the  of an element if that element contains no other nodes other than , comment nodes, and processing instruction nodes. success
