h3 4.2.4.5 Early hints
button MDN
text allow user-agents to perform some operations, such as to speculatively load resources that are likely to be used by the document, before the navigation request is fully handled by the server and a response code is served. Servers can indicate early hints by serving a  with a 103 status code before serving the final .
text Early hints
link response https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-response
link response https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-response
link [RFC8297] #refsRFC8297
text For compatibility reasons , but for readability we use HTTP/1.1-style notation below. success
link "early hints are typically delivered over HTTP/2 or above" https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc8297.html#security-considerations
text For example, given the following sequence of responses:
text 103 Early Hint Link: </image.png>; =; =image
row
  link rel #attr-link-rel
  link preload #link-type-preload
  link as #attr-link-as
text "200 OK Content-Type: text/html <!DOCTYPE html> ... <img src=\"/image.png\">"
text the image will start loading before the HTML content arrives.
text Only the first early hint response served during the navigation is handled, and it is discarded if it is succeeded by a cross-origin redirect. success
text In addition to the `` headers, it is possible that the 103 response contains a  header, which is enforced when processing the early hint.
row
  link Link https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc8288.html#header
  link "Content Security Policy" https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#content-security-policy-object
text For example, given the following sequence of responses:
text 103 Early Hint Content-Security-Policy: style-src: self; Link: </style.css>; =; =style
row
  link rel #attr-link-rel
  link preload #link-type-preload
  link as #attr-link-as
text 103 Early Hint Link: </image.png>; =; =image
row
  link rel #attr-link-rel
  link preload #link-type-preload
  link as #attr-link-as
text 302 Redirect Location: /alternate.html
text 200 OK Content-Security-Policy: style-src: none; Link: </font.ttf>; =; =font
row
  link rel #attr-link-rel
  link preload #link-type-preload
  link as #attr-link-as
text The font and style would be loaded, and the image will be discarded, as only the first early hint response in the final redirect chain is respected. The late  header comes after the request to fetch the style has already been performed, but the style will not be accessible to the document.
