text The  element  a complete, or self-contained, composition in a document, page, application, or site and that is, in principle, independently distributable or reusable, e.g. in syndication. This could be a forum post, a magazine or newspaper article, a blog entry, a user-submitted comment, an interactive widget or gadget, or any other independent item of content.
row
  link article #the-article-element
  link represents #represents
text When  elements are nested, the inner  elements represent articles that are in principle related to the contents of the outer article. For instance, a blog entry on a site that accepts user-submitted comments could represent the comments as  elements nested within the  element for the blog entry.
link article #the-article-element
link article #the-article-element
link article #the-article-element
link article #the-article-element
text Author information associated with an  element (q.v. the  element) does not apply to nested  elements.
