text The  element  a generic section of a document or application. A section, in this context, is a thematic grouping of content, typically with a heading.
row
  link section #the-section-element
  link represents #represents
text Examples of sections would be chapters, the various tabbed pages in a tabbed dialog box, or the numbered sections of a thesis. A web site's home page could be split into sections for an introduction, news items, and contact information.
text Authors are encouraged to use the  element instead of the  element when it would make sense to syndicate the contents of the element. success
row
  link article #the-article-element
  link section #the-section-element
text The  element is not a generic container element. When an element is needed only for styling purposes or as a convenience for scripting, authors are encouraged to use the  element instead. A general rule is that the  element is appropriate only if the element's contents would be listed explicitly in the document's . success
link section #the-section-element
link div #the-div-element
link section #the-section-element
link outline #outline
text In the following example, we see an article (part of a larger web page) about apples, containing two short sections.
text Apples Tasty, delicious fruit!  The apple is the pomaceous fruit of the apple tree.  Red Delicious These bright red apples are the most common found in many supermarkets.   Granny Smith These juicy, green apples make a great filling for apple pies.
