link type #attr-ol-type
link decimal #attr-ol-type-state-decimal
table Keyword State Description "Examples for values 1-3 and 3999-4001"
  1 (U+0031) | decimal | Decimal numbers | 1. | 2. | 3. | ... | 3999. | 4000. | 4001. | ...
  a (U+0061) | lower-alpha | Lowercase latin alphabet | a. | b. | c. | ... | ewu. | ewv. | eww. | ...
  A (U+0041) | upper-alpha | Uppercase latin alphabet | A. | B. | C. | ... | EWU. | EWV. | EWW. | ...
  i (U+0069) | lower-roman | Lowercase roman numerals | i. | ii. | iii. | ... | mmmcmxcix. | i̅v̅. | i̅v̅i. | ...
  I (U+0049) | upper-roman | Uppercase roman numerals | I. | II. | III. | ... | MMMCMXCIX. | I̅V̅. | I̅V̅I. | ...
text User agents should render the items of the list in a manner consistent with the state of the  attribute of the  element. Numbers less than or equal to zero should always use the decimal system regardless of the  attribute.
