h3 4.8.4.1.1 Adaptive images
text This section is non-normative.
text CSS and media queries can be used to construct graphical page layouts that adapt dynamically to the user's environment, in particular to different  dimensions and pixel densities. For content, however, CSS does not help; instead, we have the  element's  attribute and the  element. This section walks through a sample case showing how to use these features.
