text Each  object must have a . Each image in this list is identified by a tuple consisting of an , a  mode, and, if the mode is not , an . Each image furthermore has an  flag. User agents may copy entries from one  object's  to another at any time (e.g. when the  is created, user agents can add to it all the images that are loaded in other s), but must not change the keys of entries copied in this way when doing so, and must unset the  flag for the copied entry. User agents may also remove images from such lists at any time (e.g. to save memory). User agents must remove entries in the  as appropriate given higher-layer caching semantics for the resource (e.g. the HTTP `` response header) when the  flag is unset.
