h3 4.8.4.3.4 Decoding images
text Image data is usually encoded in order to reduce file size. This means that in order for the user agent to present the image to the screen, the data needs to be decoded.  is the process which converts an image's media data into a bitmap form, suitable for presentation to the screen. Note that this process can be slow relative to other processes involved in presenting content. Thus, the user agent can choose when to perform decoding, in order to create the best user experience.
text Decoding
text Image decoding is said to be synchronous if it prevents presentation of other content until it is finished. Typically, this has an effect of atomically presenting the image and any other content at the same time. However, this presentation is delayed by the amount of time it takes to perform the decode.
text Image decoding is said to be asynchronous if it does not prevent presentation of other content. This has an effect of presenting non-image content faster. However, the image content is missing on screen until the decode finishes. Once the decode is finished, the screen is updated with the image.
text In both synchronous and asynchronous decoding modes, the final content is presented to screen after the same amount of time has elapsed. The main difference is whether the user agent presents non-image content ahead of presenting the final content.
text In order to aid the user agent in deciding whether to perform synchronous or asynchronous decode, the  attribute can be set on  elements. The possible values of the  attribute are the following  keywords:
link decoding #attr-img-decoding
link img #the-img-element
link decoding #attr-img-decoding
text image decoding hint
table Keyword State Description
  sync | Sync | Indicates a preference to decode this image synchronously for atomic presentation with other content.
  async | Async | Indicates a preference to decode this image asynchronously to avoid delaying presentation of other content.
  auto | Auto | Indicates no preference in decoding mode (the default).
text When  an image, the user agent should respect the preference indicated by the  attribute's state. If the state indicated is , then the user agent is free to choose any decoding behavior.
row
