  text >
  text <
  text img success
  text src primary
  text =
  text "\"images/parsing-model-overview.svg\"" warning
  text alt primary
  text =
  text "\"The Network" warning
  text passes data to the Input Stream Preprocessor, which passes it to the warning
  text Tokenizer, which passes it to the Tree Construction stage. From there, warning
  text data goes to both the DOM and to Script Execution. Script Execution is warning
  text linked to the DOM, and, using document.write(), passes data to the warning
  text "Tokenizer.\"" warning
  text >
  text </
  text p success
  text >
text Here's another example, showing a good solution and a bad solution to the problem of including an image in a description.
text First, here's the good solution. This sample shows how the alternative text should just be what you would have put in the prose if the image had never existed.
text You are standing in an open field west of a house.  There is a small mailbox here.
