h3 4.8.4.4.11 A key part of the content
text In some cases, the image is a critical part of the content. This could be the case, for instance, on a page that is part of a photo gallery. The image is the whole point of the page containing it.
text How to provide alternative text for an image that is a key part of the content depends on the image's provenance.
text The general case
text When it is possible for detailed alternative text to be provided, for example if the image is part of a series of screenshots in a magazine review, or part of a comic strip, or is a photograph in a blog entry about that photograph, text that can serve as a substitute for the image must be given as the contents of the  attribute.
link alt #attr-img-alt
text A screenshot in a gallery of screenshots for a new OS, with some alternative text:
text Screenshot of a KDE desktop.
card
  text <
  text figure success
  text >
  text <
  text img success
  text src primary
  text =
  text "\"KDE%20Light%20desktop.png\"" warning
  text alt primary
  text =
  text "\"The desktop is blue, with icons along the left hand side in" warning
  text two columns, reading System, Home, K-Mail, etc. A window is warning
  text open showing that menus wrap to a second line if they warning
  text cannot fit in the window. The window has a list of icons warning
  text along the top, with an address bar below it, a list of warning
  text icons for tabs along the left edge, a status bar on the warning
  text bottom, and two panes in the middle. The desktop has a bar warning
  text at the bottom of the screen with a few buttons, a pager, a warning
  text "list of open applications, and a clock.\"" warning
  text >
  text <
  text figcaption success
  text >
  text </
  text figcaption success
  text >
  text </
  text figure success
  text >
text A graph in a financial report:
card
