h3 4.8.11.3 MIME types
text A  can be described in terms of its , specifically a , in some cases with a  parameter. (Whether the  parameter is allowed or not depends on the MIME type.)
link "media resource" #media-resource
text type
link "MIME type" https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-type
text codecs
text codecs
link [RFC6381] #refsRFC6381
text "Types are usually somewhat incomplete descriptions; for example \"video/mpeg\" doesn't say anything except what the container type is, and even a type like \"video/mp4; codecs=\"avc1.42E01E, mp4a.40.2\"\" doesn't include information like the actual bitrate (only the maximum bitrate). Thus, given a type, a user agent can often only know whether it might be able to play media of that type (with varying levels of confidence), or whether it definitely cannot play media of that type."
text is one that describes a resource that the user agent definitely does not support, for example because it doesn't recognize the container type, or it doesn't support the listed codecs.
text A type that the user agent knows it cannot render
text "The  \"\" with no parameters is never . User agents must treat that type as equivalent to the lack of any explicit  when it is used to label a potential ."
