text User agents may decide to not download more content at any time, e.g. after buffering five minutes of a one hour media resource, while waiting for the user to decide whether to play the resource or not, while waiting for user input in an interactive resource, or when the user navigates away from the page. When a 's download has been suspended, the user agent must  given the  to set the  to  and  named  at the element. If and when downloading of the resource resumes, the user agent must  given the  to set the  to . Between the queuing of these tasks, the load is suspended (so  events don't fire, as described above).
