text "For example, if two clips have been concatenated into one video file, but the video format exposes the original times for the two clips, the video data might expose a timeline that goes, say, 00:15..00:29 and then 00:05..00:38. However, the user agent would not expose those times; it would instead expose the times as 00:15..00:29 and 00:29..01:02, as a single video."
text In the rare case of a  that does not have an explicit timeline, the zero time on the  should correspond to the first frame of the . In the even rarer case of a  with no explicit timings of any kind, not even frame durations, the user agent must itself determine the time for each frame in an  manner.
