text "In practice, the difference between  and  is negligible. Really the only time the difference is relevant is when painting a  element onto a , where it distinguishes the case where something will be drawn ( or greater) from the case where nothing is drawn ( or less). Similarly, the difference between  (only the current frame) and  (at least this frame and the next) can be negligible (in the extreme, only one frame). The only time that distinction really matters is when a page provides an interface for \"frame-by-frame\" navigation." success
