text A readiness state
text One of the following:
text Not loaded
text Indicates that the text track's cues have not been obtained.
text Loading
text Indicates that the text track is loading and there have been no fatal errors encountered so far. Further cues might still be added to the track by the parser.
text Loaded
text Indicates that the text track has been loaded with no fatal errors.
text Failed to load
text Indicates that the text track was enabled, but when the user agent attempted to obtain it, this failed in some way (e.g.,  could not be , network error, unknown text track format). Some or all of the cues are likely missing and will not be obtained.
link URL https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url
link parsed #encoding-parsing-a-url
text The  of a  changes dynamically as the track is obtained.
row
  link "readiness state" #text-track-readiness-state
  link "text track" #text-track
text A mode
text One of the following:
text Disabled
text Indicates that the text track is not active. Other than for the purposes of exposing the track in the DOM, the user agent is ignoring the text track. No cues are active, no events are fired, and the user agent will not attempt to obtain the track's cues.
text Hidden
text Indicates that the text track is active, but that the user agent is not actively displaying the cues. If no attempt has yet been made to obtain the track's cues, the user agent will perform such an attempt momentarily. The user agent is maintaining a list of which cues are active, and events are being fired accordingly.
text Showing
text Indicates that the text track is active. If no attempt has yet been made to obtain the track's cues, the user agent will perform such an attempt momentarily. The user agent is maintaining a list of which cues are active, and events are being fired accordingly. In addition, for text tracks whose  is  or , the cues are being overlaid on the video as appropriate; for text tracks whose  is , the user agent is making the cues available to the user in a non-visual fashion; and for text tracks whose  is , the user agent is making available to the user a mechanism by which the user can navigate to any point in the  by selecting a cue.
