text A  consists of cells aligned on a two-dimensional grid of  with coordinates (, ). The grid is finite, and is either empty or has one or more slots. If the grid has one or more slots, then the  coordinates are always in the range , and the  coordinates are always in the range . If one or both of  and  are zero, then the table is empty (has no slots). Tables correspond to  elements.
