text "This requirement is a  of RFC 5322, which defines a syntax for email addresses that is simultaneously too strict (before the \"@\" character), too vague (after the \"@\" character), and too lax (allowing comments, whitespace characters, and quoted strings in manners unfamiliar to most users) to be of practical use here." success
