h3 4.11.3 Commands
h3 4.11.3.1 Facets
text A  is the abstraction behind menu items, buttons, and links. Once a command is defined, other parts of the interface can refer to the same command, allowing many access points to a single feature to share facets such as the .
text command
link "Disabled State" #command-facet-disabledstate
text Commands are defined to have the following :
text facets
text Label
text The name of the command as seen by the user.
text Access Key
text A key combination selected by the user agent that triggers the command. A command might not have an Access Key.
text Hidden State
text Whether the command is hidden or not (basically, whether it should be shown in menus).
text Disabled State
text Whether the command is relevant and can be triggered or not.
text Action
text The actual effect that triggering the command will have. This could be a scripted event handler, a  to which to , or a form submission.
