h3 4.12 Scripting
text Scripts allow authors to add interactivity to their documents.
text Authors are encouraged to use declarative alternatives to scripting where possible, as declarative mechanisms are often more maintainable, and many users disable scripting.
text For example, instead of using a script to show or hide a section to show more details, the  element could be used.
link details #the-details-element
text Authors are also encouraged to make their applications degrade gracefully in the absence of scripting support.
text For example, if an author provides a link in a table header to dynamically resort the table, the link could also be made to function without scripts by requesting the sorted table from the server.
