link defer #attr-script-defer
text This is all summarized in the following schematic diagram:
image https://html.spec.whatwg.org/images/asyncdefer.svg "With <script>, parsing is interrupted by fetching and execution. With <script defer>, fetching is parallel to parsing and execution takes place after all parsing has finished. And with <script async>, fetching is parallel to parsing but once it finishes parsing is interrupted to execute the script. The story for <script type=\"module\"> is similar to <script defer>, but the dependencies will be fetched as well, and the story for <script type=\"module\" async> is similar to <script async> with the extra dependency fetching."
text The exact processing details for these attributes are, for mostly historical reasons, somewhat non-trivial, involving a number of aspects of HTML. The implementation requirements are therefore by necessity scattered throughout the specification. The algorithms  describe the core of this processing, but these algorithms reference and are referenced by the parsing rules for   and  tags in HTML, , and , the rules for the  method, the handling of , etc. success
