text When the object implementing the  interface is created, the font of the context must be set to 10px sans-serif. When the  component is set to lengths using percentages,  or  units, or the 'larger' or 'smaller' keywords, these must be interpreted relative to the  of the  property of the  at the time that the attribute is set, if it is an element. When the  component is set to the relative values 'bolder' and 'lighter', these must be interpreted relative to the  of the  property of the  at the time that the attribute is set, if it is an element. If the  are undefined for a particular case (e.g. because the  is not an element or is not ), then the relative keywords must be interpreted relative to the normal-weight 10px sans-serif default.
