text The  attribute's allowed keywords are as follows:
link textAlign #dom-context-2d-textalign
text start
text Align to the start edge of the text (left side in left-to-right text, right side in right-to-left text).
text end
text Align to the end edge of the text (right side in left-to-right text, left side in right-to-left text).
text left
text Align to the left.
text right
text Align to the right.
text center
text Align to the center.
text The  attribute's allowed keywords correspond to alignment points in the font:
link textBaseline #dom-context-2d-textbaseline
image https://html.spec.whatwg.org/images/baselines.png "The em-over baseline is roughly at the top of the glyphs in a font, the hanging baseline is where some glyphs like आ are anchored, the middle is half-way between the em-over and em-under baselines, the alphabetic baseline is where characters like Á, ÿ, f, and Ω are anchored, the ideographic-under baseline is where glyphs like 私 and 達 are anchored, and the em-under baseline is roughly at the bottom of the glyphs in a font. The top and bottom of the bounding box can be far from these baselines, due to glyphs extending far outside em-over and em-under baselines."
text The keywords map to these alignment points as follows:
