h3 4.12.5.1.6 Building paths
text Objects that implement the  interface have a . A  has a list of zero or more subpaths. Each subpath consists of a list of one or more points, connected by straight or curved , and a flag indicating whether the subpath is closed or not. A closed subpath is one where the last point of the subpath is connected to the first point of the subpath by a straight line. Subpaths with only one point are ignored when painting the path.
