h3 4.12.5.1.23 Best practices
text When a canvas is interactive, authors should include  elements in the element's fallback content corresponding to each  part of the canvas, as in the .
link focusable #focusable
link focusable #focusable
link "example above" #drawCustomFocusRingExample
text When rendering focus rings, to ensure that focus rings have the appearance of native focus rings, authors should use the  method, passing it the element for which a ring is being drawn. This method only draws the focus ring if the element is , so that it can simply be called whenever drawing the element, without checking whether the element is focused or not first.
link drawFocusIfNeeded() #dom-context-2d-drawfocusifneeded
link focused #focused
text Authors should avoid implementing text editing controls using the  element. Doing so has a large number of disadvantages:
link canvas #the-canvas-element
text Mouse placement of the caret has to be reimplemented.
text Keyboard movement of the caret has to be reimplemented (possibly across lines, for multiline text input).
text Scrolling of the text control has to be implemented (horizontally for long lines, vertically for multiline input).
text Native features such as copy-and-paste have to be reimplemented.
text Native features such as spell-checking have to be reimplemented.
text Native features such as drag-and-drop have to be reimplemented.
text Native features such as page-wide text search have to be reimplemented.
text Native features specific to the user, for example custom text services, have to be reimplemented. This is close to impossible since each user might have different services installed, and there is an unbounded set of possible such services.
text Bidirectional text editing has to be reimplemented.
text For multiline text editing, line wrapping has to be implemented for all relevant languages.
text Text selection has to be reimplemented.
text Dragging of bidirectional text selections has to be reimplemented.
text Platform-native keyboard shortcuts have to be reimplemented.
text Platform-native input method editors (IMEs) have to be reimplemented.
text Undo and redo functionality has to be reimplemented.
text Accessibility features such as magnification following the caret or selection have to be reimplemented.
text This is a huge amount of work, and authors are most strongly encouraged to avoid doing any of it by instead using the  element, the  element, or the  attribute.
link input #the-input-element
link textarea #the-textarea-element
link contenteditable #attr-contenteditable
