text Implementations are encouraged to short-circuit the graphics update steps of the  for the purposes of updating the contents of a  to the display. This could mean, for example, that the bitmap contents are copied directly to a graphics buffer that is mapped to the physical display location of the . This or similar short-circuiting approaches can significantly reduce display latency, especially in cases where the  is updated from a  and the  of the  is busy. However, such shortcuts cannot have any script-observable side-effects. This means that the committed bitmap still needs to be sent to the , in case the element is used as a , as an , or in case  or  are called on it. success
