h3 4.13.2.1 Preserving custom element state when moved
text This section is non-normative.
text "When manipulating the DOM tree, an element can be  in the tree while connected. This applies to custom elements as well. By default, the \"\" and \"\" would be called on the element, one after the other. This is done to maintain compatibility with existing custom elements that predate the  method. This means that by default, custom elements reset their state as if they were removed and re-inserted. In the example , the impact would be that the observer would be disconnected and re-connected, and the tab index would be reset."
