text The following extract shows how an IM conversation log could be marked up, using the  element to provide Unix timestamps for each line. Note that the timestamps are provided in a format that the  element does not support, so the  element is used instead (namely, Unix  timestamps). Had the author wished to mark up the data using one of the date and time formats supported by the  element, that element could have been used instead of . This could be advantageous as it would allow data analysis tools to detect the timestamps unambiguously, without coordination with the page author.
