text For each element, user agents must establish a , either through defaults or through preferences expressed by the user. There are three possible default behaviors for each element:
text default behavior
text true-by-default
text The element will be checked for spelling and grammar if its contents are editable and spellchecking is not explicitly disabled through the  attribute.
link spellcheck #attr-spellcheck
text false-by-default
text The element will never be checked for spelling and grammar unless spellchecking is explicitly enabled through the  attribute.
link spellcheck #attr-spellcheck
text inherit-by-default
text The element's default behavior is the same as its parent element's. Elements that have no parent element cannot have this as their default behavior.
