text To determine if a word, sentence, or other piece of text in an applicable element (as defined above) is to have spelling- and grammar-checking enabled, the UA must use the following algorithm:
text If the user has disabled the checking for this text, then the checking is disabled.
text Otherwise, if the user has forced the checking for this text to always be enabled, then the checking is enabled.
text Otherwise, if the element with which the text is associated has a  content attribute, then: if that attribute is in the  state, then checking is enabled; otherwise, if that attribute is in the  state, then checking is disabled.
