text A , an algorithm accepting a boolean argument and returning a boolean. The argument indicates whether or not the cancel action algorithm can prevent the close request from proceeding via the algorithm's return value. If the boolean argument is true, then the algorithm can return either true to indicate that the caller will proceed to the , or false to indicate that the caller will bail out. If the argument is false, then the return value is always false. This algorithm can never throw an exception.
