h3 6.11.2 The drag data store
text The data that underlies a drag-and-drop operation, known as the , consists of the following information:
text drag data store
text A , which is a list of items representing the dragged data, each consisting of the following information:
text drag data store item list
text The drag data item kind
text The kind of data:
text Text
text Text.
text File
text Binary data with a filename.
text The drag data item type string
text A Unicode string giving the type or format of the data, generally given by a . Some values that are not  are special-cased for legacy reasons. The API does not enforce the use of ; other values can be used as well. In all cases, however, the values are all  by the API.
link "MIME type" https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-type
link "MIME types" https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-type
link "MIME types" https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-type
link "converted to ASCII lowercase" https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-lowercase
text There is a limit of one  item per .
row
  text text
  link "item type string" #the-drag-data-item-type-string
text The actual data
text A Unicode or binary string, in some cases with a filename (itself a Unicode string), as per .
link "the drag data item kind" #the-drag-data-item-kind
text The  is ordered in the order that the items were added to the list; most recently added last.
link "drag data store item list" #drag-data-store-item-list
text The following information, used to generate the UI feedback during the drag:
text User-agent-defined default feedback information, known as the .
text drag data store default feedback
text Optionally, a bitmap image and the coordinate of a point within that image, known as the  and .
text drag data store bitmap
