text User agents may limit the number of state objects added to the session history per page. If a page hits the  limit, user agents must remove the entry immediately after the first entry for that  object in the session history after having added the new entry. (Thus the state history acts as a FIFO buffer for eviction, but as a LIFO buffer for navigation.)
