text The  option can be a function that returns a promise. The handler function will run after the  event has finished firing and the  property has been updated. This returned promise is used to signal the duration, and success or failure, of the navigation. After it settles, the browser signals to the user (e.g., via a loading spinner UI, or assistive technology) that the navigation is finished. Additionally, it fires  or  events as appropriate, which other parts of the web application can respond to. success
