h3 7.3.1.4 Jake diagrams
text A useful method for visualizing sequences of documents, and in particular  and their , is the . A typical Jake diagram is the following:
row
  link navigables #navigable
  link "session history entries" #session-history-entry
  text Jake diagram
table Col 0 1 2 3 4
  top | /t-a | /t-a#foo | /t-b
  frames[0] | /i-0-a | /i-0-b
  frames[1] | /i-1-a | /i-1-b
text Here, each numbered column denotes a possible value for the traversable's . Each labeled row depicts a , as it transitions between different URLs and documents. The first, labeled , being the , and the others being . The documents are given by the background color of each cell, with a new background color indicating a new document in that . The URLs are given by the text content of the cells; usually they are given as  for brevity, unless a cross-origin case is specifically under investigation. A given navigable might not exist at a given step, in which case the corresponding cells are empty. The bold-italic step number depicts the  of the traversable, and all cells with bold-italic URLs represent the  for that row's navigable.
link "session history step" #tn-current-session-history-step
link navigable #navigable
