text The return values of these algorithms are ordered so that parents appears before their children. Callers rely on this ordering. success
text Starting with a , rather than a , is generally better because it makes the caller cognizant of whether they are starting with a   or not. Although non- s do have ancestor and descendant navigables, they often behave as if they don't (e.g., in the  getter). success
