text "These values have different meanings based on whether the page is sandboxed or not, as summarized in the following (non-normative) table. In this table, \"current\" means the  that the link or script is in, \"parent\" means the  of the  that the link or script is in, \"top\" means the  of the  that the link or script is in, \"new\" means a new  with a null  (which may use an , subject to various user preferences and user agent policies), \"none\" means that nothing will happen, and \"maybe new\" means the same as \"new\" if the \"\" keyword is also specified on the  attribute (or if the user overrode the sandboxing), and the same as \"none\" otherwise."
