h3 7.6 Speculative loading
text Speculative loading is the practice of performing navigation actions, such as prefetching, ahead of navigation starting. This makes subsequent navigations faster.
text Developers can initiate speculative loads by using . User agents might also perform speculative loads in certain  scenarios, such as typing into the address bar.
link "speculation rules" #speculation-rule-set
link implementation-defined https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#implementation-defined
