  text speculation rule requirement
  text anonymous-client-ip-when-cross-origin
text In the future, more possible requirements might be defined. success
h3 7.6.1.2 Parsing
text Since speculative loading is a progressive enhancement, this standard is fairly conservative in its parsing behavior. In particular, unknown keys or invalid values usually cause parsing failure, since it is safer to do nothing than to possibly misinterpret a speculation rule. success
text That said, parsing failure for a single speculation rule still allows other speculation rules to be processed. It is only in the case of top-level misconfiguration that the entire speculation rule set is discarded. success
