h3 7.6.5 Security considerations
h3 7.6.5.1 Cross-site requests
text Speculative loads can be initiated by web pages to cross-site destinations. However, because such cross-site speculative loads are always done without , as explained , ambient authority is limited to requests that are already possible via other mechanisms on the platform.
row
  link credentials https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#credentials
  link below #speculative-loading-state-partitioning
text "The `` header can also be used to issue requests, for JSON documents whose body will be . However, they use the \"\" , the \"\" , and responses which do not use the   are ignored, so they are not useful in mounting attacks."
link Speculation-Rules #speculation-rules-2
