text Entry
text This corresponds to the script that initiated the currently running script action: i.e., the function or script that the user agent called into when it called into author code.
text Incumbent
text This corresponds to the most-recently-entered author function or script on the stack, or the author function or script that originally scheduled the currently-running callback.
text Current
text This corresponds to the currently-running function object, including built-in user-agent functions which might not be implemented as JavaScript. (It is derived from the .)
link "current realm" https://tc39.es/ecma262/#current-realm
text Relevant
text Every  has a , which is roughly the  in which it was created. When writing algorithms, the most prominent  whose  might be important is the  value of the currently-running function object. In some cases, there can be other important , such as those of any arguments.
