h3 8.1.5 Module specifier resolution
h3 8.1.5.1 The resolution algorithm
text The  algorithm is the primary entry point for converting module specifier strings into . When no  are involved, it is relatively straightforward, and reduces to .
link "resolve a module specifier" #resolve-a-module-specifier
link URLs https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url
link "import maps" #import-map
link "resolving a URL-like module specifier" #resolving-a-url-like-module-specifier
text When there is a non-empty  present, the behavior is more complex. It checks candidate entries from all applicable , from most-specific to least-specific  (falling back to the top-level unscoped ), and from most-specific to least-specific prefixes. For each candidate, the  algorithm will give one of the following results:
link "import map" #import-map
link "module specifier maps" #module-specifier-map
link scopes #concept-import-map-scopes
link imports #concept-import-map-imports
link "resolve an imports match" #resolving-an-imports-match
text Successful resolution of the specifier to a . Then the  algorithm will return that URL.
row
  link URL https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url
  link "resolve a module specifier" #resolve-a-module-specifier
text Throwing an exception. Then the  algorithm will rethrow that exception, without any further fallbacks.
link "resolve a module specifier" #resolve-a-module-specifier
text Failing to resolve, without an error. In this case the outer  algorithm will move on to the next candidate.
link "resolve a module specifier" #resolve-a-module-specifier
