text The above algorithm merges a new import map into the given 's 's . Let's examine a few examples:
row
  link "environment settings object" #environment-settings-object
  link "global object" #global-object
  link "import map" #import-map
text There are two cases when rules of the new import map don't get merged into the existing one.
text "The new import map rule has the exact same scope and specifier as a rule in the existing import map. We'll call that \"conflicting rule\"."
text "The new import map rule may impact the resolution of an already resolved module. We'll call that \"impacted already resolved module\"."
text "When the new import map has no conflicting rules, and there are no impacted resolved modules, the resulting map would be a combination of the new and existing maps. Rules that would have individually impacted similar modules (e.g. \"/app/\" and \"/app/helper\") but are not an exact match are not conflicting, and all make it to the merged map."
text So, the following existing and new import maps:
card
  text {
  text "\"imports\"" warning
  text :
  text {
  text "\"/app/\"" warning
  text :
  text "\"./original-app/\"" warning
  text ,
  text }
  text }
card
  text {
  text "\"imports\"" warning
  text :
  text {
  text "\"/app/helper\"" warning
  text :
  text "\"./helper/index.mjs\"" warning
  text },
  text "\"scopes\"" warning
  text :
  text {
  text "\"/js\"" warning
  text :
  text {
  text "\"/app/\"" warning
  text :
  text "\"./js-app/\"" warning
  text }
  text }
  text }
text Would be equivalent to the following single import map:
card
  text {
  text "\"imports\"" warning
  text :
  text {
  text "\"/app/\"" warning
  text :
  text "\"./original-app/\"" warning
  text ,
  text "\"/app/helper\"" warning
  text :
  text "\"./helper/index.mjs\"" warning
  text },
  text "\"scopes\"" warning
  text :
  text {
  text "\"/js\"" warning
  text :
  text {
  text "\"/app/\"" warning
  text :
  text "\"./js-app/\"" warning
  text }
  text }
  text }
text When the new import map impacts an already resolved module, that rule gets dropped from the import map.
text "So, if the  already contains the \"\", the following new import map:"
row
  link "resolved module set" #resolved-module-set
  text /app/helper
card
