text The JavaScript specification defines Jobs to be scheduled and run later by the host, as well as  which encapsulate JavaScript functions that are called as part of jobs. The JavaScript specification contains a number of  abstract operations that lets the host define how jobs are scheduled and how JobCallbacks are handled. HTML uses these abstract operations to  by saving and restoring the  and a  for the  in JobCallbacks. This section defines them for user agent hosts.
