text For example, a user agent could have one  for mouse and key events (to which the  is associated), and another to which all other  are associated. Then, using the freedom granted in the initial step of the , it could give keyboard and mouse events preference over other tasks three-quarters of the time, keeping the interface responsive but not starving other task queues. Note that in this setup, the processing model still enforces that the user agent would never process events from any one  out of order.
