text visible
text This specification does not mandate any particular model for selecting rendering opportunities. But for example, if the browser is attempting to achieve a 60Hz refresh rate, then rendering opportunities occur at a maximum of every 60th of a second (about 16.7ms). If the browser finds that a  is not able to sustain this rate, it might drop to a more sustainable 30 rendering opportunities per second for that , rather than occasionally dropping frames. Similarly, if a  is not visible, the user agent might decide to drop that page to a much slower 4 rendering opportunities per second, or even less. success
