text Set .[[ScriptOrModule]] to null.
text function
text This is done because the default behavior, of associating the created function with the nearest  on the stack, can lead to path-dependent results. For example, an event handler which is first invoked by user interaction would end up with null [[ScriptOrModule]] (since then this algorithm would be first invoked when the  is null), whereas one that is first invoked by dispatching an event from script would have its [[ScriptOrModule]] set to that script. success
link script #concept-script
link "active script" #active-script
text Instead, we just always set [[ScriptOrModule]] to null. This is more intuitive anyway; the idea that the first script which dispatches an event is somehow responsible for the event handler code is dubious. success
text In practice, this only affects the resolution of relative URLs via , which consult the  of the associated script. Nulling out [[ScriptOrModule]] means that  will fall back to the 's . success
