text This diverges from the DOM insertion methods (such as ), which only reject such insertions when the resulting tree would be invalid, and from , which allows inserting adjacent to a child of a  element or inside an  element. The  require an  context for the fragment parser, which a  or hostless  cannot provide, and they treat a  element as standing for its  rather than its , so inserting adjacent to the latter is disallowed. Similarly,  and  disallow an  element as the parent, because parsing a fragment with an  context element always produces both a  and a  element, which is only suitable when replacing all children via  or . Additionally, while legacy methods such as  and  throw a   when the parent is a , the  throw a   instead. success
