link "built-in safe default configuration" #built-in-safe-default-configuration
text Not all configuration dictionaries are valid. A valid configuration avoids redundancy (like specifying the same element to be allowed twice) and contradictions (like specifying an element to be both removed and allowed.)
text Several conditions need to hold for a configuration to be valid:
text Mixing global allow- and remove-lists:
text or  can exist, but not both. If both are missing, this is equivalent to  being an empty list.
