link Document.parseHTML() #dom-parsehtml
text If a developer were to retrieve a sanitized node tree as a string, e.g. via , and to then parse it again then mutation XSS can occur. This practice is strongly discouraged. If processing or passing of HTML as a string is necessary after all, then any string is to be considered untrusted and re-sanitized when inserted into the DOM. In other words, a sanitized and then serialized HTML tree can no longer be considered sanitized. A more complete treatment of mXSS can be found in .
link innerHTML #dom-element-innerhtml
link [MXSS] #refsMXSS
