h3 10.1.2.4 Shared state using a shared worker
text This section is non-normative.
text In this example, multiple windows (viewers) can be opened that are all viewing the same map. All the windows share the same map information, with a single worker coordinating all the viewers. Each viewer can move around independently, but if they set any data on the map, all the viewers are updated.
text The main page isn't interesting, it merely provides a way to open the viewers:
text Workers example: Multiviewer   openViewer  windowopen       Open a new viewer Each viewer opens in a new window. You can have as many viewers as you like, they all view the same data.
