row
  text Connecting to multiple pages
  link onconnect #handler-sharedworkerglobalscope-onconnect
text "Direct channels. When the worker receives a \"msg\" message from one viewer naming another viewer, it sets up a direct connection between the two, so that the two viewers can communicate directly without the worker having to proxy all the messages."
text .
link "View this example online" /demos/workers/multiviewer/page.html
h3 10.1.2.5 Delegation
text This section is non-normative.
text With multicore CPUs becoming prevalent, one way to obtain better performance is to split computationally expensive tasks amongst multiple workers. In this example, a computationally expensive task that is to be performed for every number from 1 to 10,000,000 is farmed out to ten subworkers.
text The main page is as follows, it just reports the result:
text Worker example: Multicore computation   Result:     worker   Worker workeronmessage   event  documentgetElementByIdtextContent  eventdata
