text They receive two numbers in two events, perform the computation for the range of numbers thus specified, and then report the result back to the parent.
text .
link "View this example online" /demos/workers/multicore/page.html
h3 10.1.2.6 Providing libraries
text This section is non-normative.
text Suppose that a cryptography library is made available that provides three tasks:
text Generate a public/private key pair
text Takes a port, on which it will send two messages, first the public key and then the private key.
text Given a plaintext and a public key, return the corresponding ciphertext
text Takes a port, to which any number of messages can be sent, the first giving the public key, and the remainder giving the plaintext, each of which is encrypted and then sent on that same channel as the ciphertext. The user can close the port when it is done encrypting content.
text Given a ciphertext and a private key, return the corresponding plaintext
text Takes a port, to which any number of messages can be sent, the first giving the private key, and the remainder giving the ciphertext, each of which is decrypted and then sent on that same channel as the plaintext. The user can close the port when it is done decrypting content.
text The library itself is as follows:
text handleMessagee   edata   genkeyseports   edata   encrypteports   edata   decrypteports   genkeysp   keys  _generateKeyPair ppostMessagekeys ppostMessagekeys   encryptp   key state   ponmessage   e   state    key  edata state      ppostMessage_encryptkey edata     decryptp   key state   ponmessage   e   state    key  edata state      ppostMessage_decryptkey edata          onmessage  handleMessage   onconnect   e  eportonmessage  handleMessage    _generateKeyPair   Mathrandom Mathrandom   _encryptk s     k    s   _decryptk s   ssubstrsindexOf
