h3 10.1.3.3 Shared workers
button ✔MDN
text This section is non-normative.
text Shared workers are identified by the URL of the script used to create it, optionally with an explicit name. The name allows multiple instances of a particular shared worker to be started.
text Shared workers are scoped by . Two different sites using the same names will not collide. However, if a page tries to use the same shared worker name as another page on the same site, but with a different script URL, it will fail.
link origin #concept-origin
text Creating shared workers is done using the  constructor. This constructor takes the URL to the script to use for its first argument, and the name of the worker, if any, as the second argument.
link SharedWorker() #dom-sharedworker
text worker   SharedWorker
