h3 13.1.2.5 Restrictions on content models
text For historical reasons, certain elements have extra restrictions beyond even the restrictions given by their content model.
text A  element must not contain  elements, even though these elements are technically allowed inside  elements according to the content models described in this specification. (If a  element is put inside a  in the markup, it will in fact imply a  start tag before it.)
