text "Otherwise, restart the  algorithm, with  set to \"\" and other inputs kept the same, but this time skip the  and instead just set the encoding to the new encoding and the  to . Whenever possible, this should be done without actually contacting the network layer (the bytes should be re-parsed from memory), even if, e.g., the document is marked as not being cacheable. If this is not possible and contacting the network layer would involve repeating a request that uses a method other than ``, then instead set the  to  and ignore the new encoding. The resource will be misinterpreted. User agents may notify the user of the situation, to aid in application development."
