h3 13.2.5 Tokenization
text Implementations must act as if they used the following state machine to tokenize HTML. The state machine must start in the . Most states consume a single character, which may have various side-effects, and either switches the state machine to a new state to  the , or switches it to a new state to consume the , or stays in the same state to consume the next character. Some states have more complicated behavior and can consume several characters before switching to another state. In some cases, the tokenizer state is also changed by the tree construction stage.
link "data state" #data-state
link reconsume #reconsume
