text "In the non-conforming stream , the first  element would be closed upon seeing the second one, and the \"x\" character would be inside a link to \"b\", not to \"a\". This is despite the fact that the outer  element is not in table scope (meaning that a regular  end tag at the start of the table wouldn't close the outer  element). The result is that the two  elements are indirectly nested inside each other — non-conforming markup will often result in non-conforming DOMs when parsed."
text "<a href=\"a\">a<table><a href=\"b\">b</table>x"
