text XML documents may contain a DOCTYPE if desired, but this is not required to conform to this specification. This specification does not define a public or system identifier, nor provide a formal DTD.
text According to , XML processors are not guaranteed to process the external DTD subset referenced in the DOCTYPE. This means, for example, that using  for characters in XML documents is unsafe if they are defined in an external file (except for , , , , and ). success
