text User agents are encouraged to ignore the  attribute and instead process the value given to the metadata name as if it had been specified for each expected value of the  attribute.
link scheme #attr-meta-scheme
link scheme #attr-meta-scheme
text "For example, if the user agent acts on  elements with  attributes having the value \"eGMS.subject.keyword\", and knows that the  attribute is used with this metadata name, then it could take the  attribute into account, acting as if it was an extension of the  attribute. Thus the following two  elements could be treated as two elements giving values for two different metadata names, one consisting of a combination of \"eGMS.subject.keyword\" and \"LGCL\", and the other consisting of a combination of \"eGMS.subject.keyword\" and \"ORLY\":"
